# __EXP_NAME__

Regional CoLM DLB factorial suite. Creation only rendered configuration; it did not create cases, run CoLM/OpenBench, or submit jobs.

## Manual gates

1. `bash config/jobs/submit_batch.sh --dry-run --stage spinup` then explicitly use `--submit`.
2. After spinup validation: `python __TOOLS_DIR__/dlb_05_restart_handoff.py prepare-dam-init --nml-dir config/colm --apply`.
3. Submit `dam-init`, validate it, then run the handoff dry-run and explicit `--apply`.
4. Submit `experiments`.
5. Activate the OpenBench environment; preview `bash config/openbench_jobs/submit_openbench_all.sh`, then explicitly add `--submit`.
6. Record OpenBench results and refresh metadata with `python __TOOLS_DIR__/dlb_07_refresh_experiment.py __EXP_DIR__`.

## Regenerate one component

- CoLM namelists and jobs: `python __TOOLS_DIR__/dlb_02_generate_namelists.py --experiment-dir __EXP_DIR__ --overwrite`
- OpenBench YAML only: `python __TOOLS_DIR__/dlb_08_generate_openbench.py __EXP_DIR__ --overwrite`

Both commands back up the replaced configuration under `provenance/backups/`.

No scheduler dependency is created automatically.

## OpenBench submission entries

Creation generates 11 `.sh` entries in `config/openbench_jobs/` without requiring
OpenBench to be installed or active. Entries locate this experiment from their own directory.

- Per group: `submit_openbench_D.sh`, `submit_openbench_L.sh`, `submit_openbench_B.sh`, `submit_openbench_DL.sh`, `submit_openbench_DB.sh`, `submit_openbench_LB.sh`, `submit_openbench_DLB.sh`, `submit_openbench_ctl.sh`, `submit_openbench_spinup.sh`, `submit_openbench_comparisons.sh`.
- All ten groups: `submit_openbench_all.sh` submits one combined array, including ctl, spinup and comparisons. Choose either all or individual groups for the same tasks to avoid duplicate submissions.

```bash
bash config/openbench_jobs/submit_openbench_D.sh --dry-run
bash config/openbench_jobs/submit_openbench_D.sh --submit
bash config/openbench_jobs/submit_openbench_all.sh --dry-run
bash config/openbench_jobs/submit_openbench_all.sh --submit
```

Default mode is preview. Only `--submit` calls LSF `bsub`; `--dry-run` and `--submit`
are mutually exclusive. Activate OpenBench first or pass `--openbench-exe /path/to/openbench`.
Entries accept resource options, `--out-dir`, `--log-dir`, `--overwrite`,
`--retry-failed` and `--rerun-unverified`; experiment selectors are fixed.
OpenBench resources use `dlb_09` defaults or invocation options, independently of CoLM.
Existing array snapshots retain their resources unless regenerated with `--overwrite`.
The `.lsf`, mapping and snapshot are generated/reused when an entry runs.
`--out-dir` changes array output only; entries stay in `config/openbench_jobs/`.
Existing identical entries are reused; different content requires `--overwrite`.
